WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.537
ROW_NUMBER assigns a unique sequence even when values tie.

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:10.332
This makes it useful for selecting exactly the top two or top three rows per group.

00:00:10.332 --> 00:00:18.212
But if salaries tie and you only order by salary, the sequence among tied rows may not be deterministic.

00:00:18.212 --> 00:00:23.382
Add a stable tie-breaker such as employee ID when the order matters.

00:00:23.382 --> 00:00:27.267
Ranking functions differ mainly in how they handle ties.

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:34.877
ROW_NUMBER forces a unique sequence, RANK leaves gaps after ties, and DENSE_RANK does not.

00:00:34.877 --> 00:00:38.857
Add deterministic tie-breakers when a unique order matters;

00:00:38.857 --> 00:00:43.509
otherwise two executions can choose different rows among tied values.
